  message: "Closed by PR #277 (merged selfh/dev 6c56e1e98b). Deleted all 29 dead producer bare-hex fingerprint sites (source[start:end] sha256) across the 10 named analyzers — cuda/fortran/glsl/graphql/nix/r_lang (lang-common), verilog/vhdl (lang-extended1), dockerfile/make (lang-mainstream) — replaced with fingerprint=None (mirroring the WGSL fix), letting the central stamp_symbol_fingerprints be the sole producer; removed 2 now-unused 'import hashlib' (verilog/vhdl). The r_lang.py file-path-hash site (a file-node fingerprint, NOT source-byte) was verified per the caveat and deliberately left intact. Pure hygiene confirmed: re-measurement showed 0 real leaks in output (all 219 non-canonical fingerprints are Class-B language=None identity-hash stand-ins the normalizer preserves by design). DELIVERED THE OPTIONAL HARDENING TOO: new _check_fingerprint_format spec-validator predicate (id_format class, content-gated, wired + wired_checks manifest + drift guard) asserts every non-null Symbol.fingerprint on a real source node (language is not None) carries the canonical hgfp2: prefix — the standing output-boundary format guard that makes a future producer/normalization bare-hex regression trip CI. Behavioral evidence: _check_fingerprint_format over the real self-analysis (35267 nodes) = 0 violations; targeted suite 100% coverage. CHANGELOG WGSL '4 emit sites'->3 nit: deferred (separate doc). No bakeoff tag (directly-verified format property)."  # e86b
